From 91112dceedbef7aac31e3da07582841cefa88455 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 1aeo <github@1aeo.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 22:42:39 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] mainloop: Keep each linked connection's index in the
 active list

connection_stop_reading_from_linked_conn() took a connection off
active_linked_connection_lst with smartlist_remove(), and
connection_start_reading_from_linked_conn() and connection_unlink()
checked membership or removed with a scan. The list holds every linked
connection that currently has data to move, and these functions run on
every read or write toggle of a linked connection, so under a flood of
short-lived BEGIN_DIR streams one of these scans can dominate the main
thread: a profile of a relay under such a flood put about 50% of its
main thread's user-space CPU in the scan in
connection_stop_reading_from_linked_conn() alone.

The code already tracked membership with the active_on_link flag; the
note there said an index was not worth it because it did not show up on
profiles. Under this flood it does. Add active_linked_conn_index beside
the flag, remove with smartlist_del() and fix the moved connection's
index, and keep the flag and index in step. connection_unlink() removes
through the same helper instead of its own scan, and connection_free_()
gains an O(1) check that the connection it frees is off the list.
connection_in_active_linked_list() replaces the open-coded membership
checks; a unit test cross-checks the index against a scan of the list,
including both sides of a linked-pair teardown.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 changes/mainloop_active_linked_index |  7 ++
 src/core/mainloop/connection.c       |  7 +-
 src/core/mainloop/mainloop.c         | 64 ++++++++++++++----
 src/core/mainloop/mainloop.h         |  3 +
 src/core/or/connection_st.h          |  3 +
 src/test/test_mainloop.c             | 97 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 6 files changed, 167 insertions(+), 14 deletions(-)
